4vl|v|To request; to seek to obtain by words; to petition; to solicit; -- often with of, in the sense of from, before the person addressed. ; To require, demand, claim, or expect, whether by way of remuneration or return, or as a matter of necessity; as, what price do you ask? ; To interrogate or inquire of or concerning; to put a question to or about; to question. ; To invite; as, to ask one to an entertainment. ; To publish in church for marriage; -- said of both the banns and the persons. ; To request or petition; -- usually followed by for; as, to ask for bread. ; To make inquiry, or seek by request; -- sometimes followed by after.	o:1njd,16,6~1njd,16,6	d:1431,7,6;1e0i,4,3;21r7,3,4~1431,7,6;21r7,3,4;1e0i,4,3	D:xkb,23,6;21tt,8,4~xkb,23,6;21tt,8,4
