52y|v|To take to or upon one's self; to take formally and demonstratively; sometimes, to appropriate or take unjustly. ; To take for granted, or without proof; to suppose as a fact; to suppose or take arbitrarily or tentatively. ; To pretend to possess; to take in appearance. ; To receive or adopt. ; To be arrogant or pretentious; to claim more than is due. ; To undertake, as by a promise.	d:1431,23,6~1431,23,6
